Slot 001 is spent, not free.

001_prune_prefix_duplicate_indexes.sql dropped the two redundant indexes on
`extension_migrations` (`idx_extension_migrations_ext_id` and
`idx_extension_migrations_ext_version`, both inside the UNIQUE constraint on
the same columns). Its end state is the declarative `schema/extension_migrations.sql`,
which has never declared either index, so a fresh database reaches it from the
base schema alone and the migration carried nothing a fresh install needed.

It ran on every fresh install anyway: the ledger table it lives in is owned by
this extension and was counted before freshness was assessed, so `database` was
never fresh and the migration took the established path. Every deployment that
needed it has it stamped or applied; the file is retired and the slot recorded
here so `ls` cannot make 001 look free.

Numbering continues at the highest slot ever used, never at the first gap.
